oncern for Fortunato’s cough, subtly guiding him toward a hidden recess where he chains him to the wall with iron staples. Montresor then methodically walls up the niche with stone and mortar, brick by brick, while Fortunato’s initial laughter turns to desperate pleas and finally silence, leaving the narrator to seal the tomb and restore the bones over it, ensuring no one will disturb the grave for fifty years.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"characters\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"char_amontillado_1b7d65f7\",\n      \"canonical_name\": \"Amontillado\",\n      \"aliases\": [],\n      \"role\": null,\n      \"appearance\": null,\n      \"personality\": null,\n      \"voice_guidance\": null,\n      \"descriptions\": [\n        {\n          \"text\": \"The narrator is a first-person storyteller recounting a past event involving a man named Fortunato. He claims to have purchased a pipe of Amontillado and seeks to verify its authenticity, leading Fortunato into a series of underground vaults. Throughout the narrative, the narrator maintains a calm, calculated demeanor while orchestrating a deliberate and secretive journey, culminating in a revelation that suggests a hidden, possibly fatal, intent.\",\n          \"source_position\": 2046,\n          \"chapter_index\": null,\n          \"confidence\": \"llm_refined\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"relationships\": {},\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"statement\": \"The narrator claims to have purchased a pipe of Amontillado\",\n          \"quote\": \"I have received a pipe of what passes for Amontillado, and I have my doubts.\",\n          \"position\": 2100,\n          \"confidence\": \"low\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"statement\": \"The narrator expresses doubt about the authenticity of the Amontillado\",\n          \"quote\": \"I have my doubts.\",\n          \"position\": 2100,\n          \"confidence\": \"low\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"statement\": \"The narrator mentions he paid the full Amontillado price without consulting Fortunato\",\n          \"quote\": \"I was silly enough to pay the full Amontillado price without consulting you in the matter.\",\n          \"position\": 2100,\n          \"confidence\": \"low\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"statement\": \"The narrator suggests he is going to consult Luchresi, implying Fortunato is the preferred expert\",\n          \"quote\": \"As you are engaged, I am on my way to Luchresi. If any one has a critical turn it is he.\",\n          \"position\": 2365,\n          \"confidence\": \"low\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"statement\": \"The narrator dismisses Luchresi's ability to distinguish Amontillado from Sherry\",\n          \"quote\": \"Luchresi cannot distinguish Sherry from Amontillado.\",\n          \"position\": 2446,\n          \"confidence\": \"low\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"statement\": \"The narrator leads Fortunato into damp, nitre-encrusted vaults\",\n          \"quote\": \"The vaults are insufferably damp. They are encrusted with nitre.\",\n          \"position\": 3108,\n          \"confidence\": \"low\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"statement\": \"The narrator insists on proceeding despite Fortunato's discomfort\",\n          \"quote\": \"Let us go, nevertheless. The cold is merely nothing.\",\n          \"position\": 3108,\n          \"confidence\": \"low\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"statement\": \"The narrator refers to the Amontillado as the ultimate goal of their journey\",\n          \"quote\": \"But let us proceed to the Amontillado.\",\n          \"position\": 7442,\n          \"confidence\": \"low\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"statement\": \"The narrator performs actions involving building stone and mortar among bones\",\n          \"quote\": \"Throwing them aside, I soon uncovered a quantity of building stone and mortar. With these...\",\n          \"position\": 9696,\n          \"confidence\": \"low\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"statement\": \"The narrator laughs in a mocking tone after the final revelation\",\n          \"quote\": \"Ha! ha! ha! --he! he! he! --a very good joke, indeed --an excellent jest.\",\n          \"position\": 12110,\n          \"confidence\": \"low\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"voice_notes\": null,\n      \"first_appearance_chapter\": 1,\n      \"mention_count\": 16,\n      \"confidence\": \"low\",\n      \"is_narrator\": false,\n      \"narrative_role\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"char_fortunato_b564181f\",\n      \"canonical_name\": \"Fortunato\",\n      \"aliases\": [],\n      \"role\": null,\n      \"appearance\": null,\n      \"personality\": null,\n      \"voice_guidance\": null,\n      \"descriptions\": [\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Fortunato is a prideful and intoxicated individual whose confidence in his wine expertise is exploited by Montresor as part of a meticulously planned murder. Initially portrayed as a carefree reveler during the carnival, his demeanor shifts from amusement to terror as he realizes he is being trapped, revealing his vulnerability and desperation in the face of impending death.\",\n          \"source_position\": 88,\n          \"chapter_index\": null,\n          \"confidence\": \"llm_refined\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"relationships\": {},\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"statement\": \"Fortunato is the target of Montresor's revenge due to an insult\",\n          \"quote\": \"The thousand injuries of Fortunato I had borne as I best could, but when he ventured upon insult I vowed revenge.\",\n          \"position\": 88,\n          \"confidence\": \"high\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"statement\": \"Fortunato is easily manipulated through his pride in wine knowledge\",\n          \"quote\": \"He prided himself on his connoisseurship in wine. Few Italians have the true virtuoso spirit.\",\n          \"position\": 921,\n          \"confidence\": \"high\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"statement\": \"Fortunato is intoxicated and unaware of the danger he is in\",\n          \"quote\": \"He had a weak point -- this Fortunato -- although in other regards he was a man to be respected and even feared.\",\n          \"position\": 921,\n          \"confidence\": \"high\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"statement\": \"Fortunato is deceived by Montresor's feigned concern\",\n          \"quote\": \"I said to him --\\\"My dear Fortunato, you are luckily met. How remarkably well you are looking to-day. But I have received a pipe of what passes for Amontillado, and I have my doubts.\\\"\",\n          \"position\": 1924,\n          \"confidence\": \"high\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"statement\": \"Fortunato continues to jest even as he is being walled in\",\n          \"quote\": \"\\\"Ha! ha! ha! --he! he! he! --a very good joke, indeed --an excellent jest. We will have many a rich laugh about it at the palazzo --he! he! he! --over our wine --he! he! he!\\\"\",\n          \"position\": 11900,\n          \"confidence\": \"high\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"statement\": \"Fortunato pleads for mercy as he realizes his fate\",\n          \"quote\": \"\\\"For the love of God, Montresor!\\\"\",\n          \"position\": 12266,\n          \"confidence\": \"high\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"statement\": \"Fortunato's final moments are marked by silence and despair\",\n          \"quote\": \"No answer still. I thrust a torch through the remaining aperture and let it fall within. There came forth in return only a jingling of the bells.\",\n          \"position\": 12506,\n          \"confidence\": \"high\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"voice_notes\": null,\n      \"first_appearance_chapter\": 1,\n      \"mention_count\": 14,\n      \"confidence\": \"high\",\n      \"is_narrator\": false,\n      \"narrative_role\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"char_montresor_dcb3c455\",\n      \"canonical_name\": \"Montresor\",\n      \"aliases\": [],\n      