hrough the damp, bone-strewn vaults, Amontillado feigns concern for Fortunato’s health, offering wine to mask the growing presence of nitre and subtly manipulate his victim’s movements.\\n\\nThe descent into the catacombs marks the turning point in the story, as Amontillado leads Fortunato deeper into the labyrinthine recesses of his ancestral home. With calculated precision, he chains Fortunato to the wall in a hidden niche, using iron staples to secure him in place. As the walls begin to rise—brick by brick—Amontillado’s calm demeanor contrasts sharply with Fortunato’s escalating panic. What begins as laughter and mockery from Fortunato slowly gives way to desperate pleas and silence, as the final stone is laid and the tomb sealed. Amontillado takes satisfaction in the completeness of his revenge, ensuring the grave will remain undisturbed for fifty years.\\n\\nThe climax occurs not in violence, but in the quiet, methodical execution of the murder, where Amontillado’s cold intellect and patience triumph over Fortunato’s arrogance. The resolution lies in the narrator’s retrospective narration, delivered with eerie calm and a sense of finality. He reflects on the success of his plan, the silence of the tomb, and the enduring nature of his vengeance. The story ends with Amontillado’s assurance that no one will ever disturb the grave, underscoring the permanence of his act and the psychological weight of his crime. The relationship between the two men—once perhaps friends or acquaintances—has been utterly transformed into one of predator and prey, with Fortunato’s pride sealing his fate.\",\n      \"themes\": [\n        \"revenge\",\n        \"deception\",\n        \"madness\"\n      ],\n      \"narrative_style\": \"first-person retrospective\"\n    },\n    \"model_usage\": {\n      \"Chapter Detection\": {\n        \"model\": \"qwen3:30b-instruct\",\n        \"provider\": \"ollama\"\n      },\n      \"Character Extraction\": {\n        \"model\": \"qwen3-next:80b-a3b